name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q5_2026'

question 'A QA Engineer is testing a fitness app. They tap "Log Run" and the run count goes up by 2 instead of 1. They ask AI to suggest a fix. AI returns a confident answer that looks reasonable. What should the QA Engineer do before trusting the fix?'

right 'Predict what the fix should do, read the AI''s code line by line, test it, and only then decide whether to accept, adapt, or reject it.'
wrong 'Apply the fix immediately because AI is usually right.'
wrong 'Reject the fix without reading it because AI can hallucinate.'
wrong 'Restart the app and hope the bug goes away.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

